  "critical": false,
  "description": "Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs): design, construction, and operation of powered aircraft with no onboard human pilot. Encompasses fixed-wing drones, multirotor quadcopters/hexacopters, and autonomous flight control systems. UAVs are the simplest powered aircraft — no cockpit, no life-support, no pilot weight — trading manned flight complexity for electronics, sensor fusion, and software. Enables aerial photography, survey, agriculture, delivery, and search-and-rescue without risking a pilot.",
